In a distributed data store during a network partition (P), you must choose between **Consistency (C)** (every read receives the most recent write or an error) and **Availability (A)** (every non-failing node returns a non-error response without guarantee of latest write).

```python
# Conceptual CAP check in distributed nodes
def read_record(node, key):
    if node.is_partitioned():
        # CAP Trade-off: Return stale data (AP) or throw error (CP)
        raise PartitionError("Node isolated - CP enforced")
    return node.storage.get(key)
